<title>VIETNAM: Vietnam sells 150 bln dong T-notes, rate 11.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Vietnam sells 150 bln dong T-notes, rate 11.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HANOI 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vietnam sold 150 billion dong ($12.85 million) worth of one-year Treasury notes with an annual coupon of 11.0 percent to domestic and foreign institutions at an auction on Wednesday, an official at the State Bank of Vietnam said.</p>
<p>At the last sale of government paper, on July 2, the central bank sold 150 billion dong worth of one-year notes at a rate of 11.15 percent.  </p>
<p>The issue date of the notes sold on Wednesday is July 11 and maturity will be on July 11, 1998.</p>
<p>The bank said allotments of stock, in dong, were as follows:</p>
<p> Industrial and Commercial Bank of Vietnam	 73.2 billion</p>
<p> Bank for Foreign Trade of Vietnam (Vietcombank) 60.0 billion</p>
<p> Asia-Pacific Commercial Joint-Stock Bank	   5.0 billion</p>
<p> Vietnam General Insurance Corporation (Bao Viet) 4.0 billion</p>
<p> National Reinsurance Company			   3.1 billion</p>
<p> Standard Chartered Bank				  2.7 billion</p>
<p> Petrolimex Joint-Stock Insurance Company	   2.0 billion</p>
<p>($1 = 11,670 dong)</p>
</text>
